{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.17b0ac7ff2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-16","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Haddad is a psychologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Haddad had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Haddad found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Haddad concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Haddad had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Psychologist Felipe Haddad set out to learn whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.","Haddad concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","Haddad found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.eee71e2c0b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-44","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Takeda is a geologist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.</li><li>Takeda measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.</li><li>Takeda found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.</li><li>Takeda concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Takeda concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","To investigate the question, Takeda measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.","Takeda found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.","Geologist Ravi Takeda set out to learn whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.4757531156","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-55","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Castellano is a zoologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Castellano gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Castellano found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Castellano concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Castellano gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Castellano found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.","Castellano concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Zoologist Kofi Castellano set out to learn whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.66afeb7943","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-59","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Haddad is a zoologist.</li><li>Haddad wanted to find out whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active.</li><li>Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.</li><li>Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.</li><li>Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Haddad found that elephants with puzzle feeders walked noticeably more each day.","To investigate the question, Haddad gave puzzle feeders to some elephants and standard food trays to others, then tracked their movement.","Haddad concluded that puzzle feeders may encourage healthy activity.","Zoologist Ingrid Haddad set out to learn whether zoo elephants that are given puzzle feeders are more active."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.4507daf9eb","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-69","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Felipe Varga is a linguist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Varga gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Varga found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Varga concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Linguist Felipe Varga set out to learn whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.","Varga concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","To investigate the question, Varga gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.","Varga found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.72623d5a5a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-75","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Varga is an economist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Varga tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Varga found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Varga concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Varga tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.","Economist Tomás Varga set out to learn whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.","Varga concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.","Varga found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.86c5b64ba6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-76","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Beatriz Rahman is an economist.</li><li>Rahman wanted to find out whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.</li><li>Rahman tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.</li><li>Rahman found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.</li><li>Rahman concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Rahman found that output per employee stayed the same or rose slightly.","To investigate the question, Rahman tracked output at companies before and after they adopted a four-day week.","Economist Beatriz Rahman set out to learn whether a four-day workweek changes employee productivity.","Rahman concluded that shorter workweeks may not reduce productivity."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.3c62577608","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-78","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Abara is a botanist.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Abara grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Abara found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Abara concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Abara concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","Abara found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","To investigate the question, Abara grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Botanist Ayumi Abara set out to learn whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.3aa96d93dd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-81","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Viktor Mensah is a botanist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Mensah grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Mensah found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Mensah concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Mensah grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Mensah found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","Mensah concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","Botanist Viktor Mensah set out to learn whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.21afca3a62","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-87","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kwame Mensah is an urban planner.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Mensah measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Mensah found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Mensah concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Urban planner Kwame Mensah set out to learn whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.","To investigate the question, Mensah measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.","Mensah found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","Mensah concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.ad3db7f6e8","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-93","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Sato is a hydrologist.</li><li>Sato wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Sato compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Sato found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Sato concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Hydrologist Elias Sato set out to learn whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.","Sato found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","To investigate the question, Sato compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Sato concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.be6273d72e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-107","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Diego Halvorsen is a chemist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Halvorsen placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Halvorsen found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Halvorsen placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Chemist Diego Halvorsen set out to learn whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.","Halvorsen found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Halvorsen concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.022c82bbf8","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-128","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Moreau is a public health researcher.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Moreau counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Moreau found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Public health researcher Zara Moreau set out to learn whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.","Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Moreau found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","To investigate the question, Moreau counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added."],"answer":"A","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.f00ac6d799","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-131","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Samuel Novak is a public health researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Novak counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.","Novak found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.","Novak concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Public health researcher Samuel Novak set out to learn whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.31847c1cf9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-154","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Mensah is a climate scientist.</li><li>Mensah wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Mensah compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Mensah found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Mensah concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Mensah found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","Mensah concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","To investigate the question, Mensah compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Climate scientist Ingrid Mensah set out to learn whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures."],"answer":"D","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.1.2cb6644380","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":1,"tmpl":"rw_synthesis.build_studies","group":"syn-s-166","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Amara Iyer is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Iyer wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Iyer played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Iyer found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Iyer concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present the aim of the study.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Iyer found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.","Veterinary scientist Amara Iyer set out to learn whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.","Iyer concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","To investigate the question, Iyer played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs."],"answer":"B","explanation":"It states what the study set out to learn. The others describe how it was done, what was found, or what was concluded."}
